  "synthesis": {
    "description": "Employees submit expense reports in the Concur expense system, which emails the approving manager that a report is ready for approval and later that its approval status has changed. The manager opens the report, reviews it and approves or rejects it. Company announcements push staff to file outstanding expenses through the XMS system and to clear reports waiting in approvers' inboxes.",
    "steps": [
      "An employee files an expense report in the expense system.",
      "The system emails the approver that the report is ready for approval.",
      "The approver opens the report and checks the items and receipts.",
      "The approver approves or rejects it, and the system emails the status change."
    ],
    "approach": "The expense system already sends the notifications; an approver checklist and automatic policy checks on receipts, limits and coding would leave the approver reviewing only flagged items, and a delegate approver could cover absences.",
    "rationale": "The work is a short review against policy each time; a checklist makes it consistent, and naming a delegate addresses the one stall the mail shows.",
    "artifact_type": "checklist"
  },
  "formula": {
